// USGS 3DEP DEM — THE UPPER MOUNTAIN, baked from pois/palisades-upper/.
// UPPER MOUNTAIN INCREMENT 1. The merged world's westernmost elevation data
// stopped at x = -1851.9 (red-dog/dem-wide's west edge). The Gold Coast bench
// is at x = -2932 and the Funitel's top terminal stands on it, so this
// increment could not be built at all without new 3DEP.
//
// Three frames, generated by work/bake_dem_upper.py:
//
//   DEM_UP_WIDE  upper/dem-wide      3600 m, 1024 -> 512 px = 7.031 m/px
//                the west surround. DECIMATED 2x1 (block mean) because the only
//                grid that reads it is terrain-wide-w at 38 m; native is 3.5156.
//   DEM_UP_W     upper/dem-tight-w   1400 m, 1024 px = 1.3672 m/px  FULL NATIVE
//                Gold Coast, High Camp, Riviera — the bench. Mean slope 17.2 deg,
//                the flattest ground in the Palisades family.
//   DEM_UP_E     upper/dem-tight-e   1400 m, 1024 px = 1.3672 m/px  FULL NATIVE
//                the Funitel's wall and Mountain Run's middle third. Mean slope
//                28.3 deg, 14.7% over 40 — the steep one.
//
// THE LATTICE IS EXACT. Each tight tile is a Mercator square of the identical
// W = 1806.354764 m as red-dog/dem-tight, offset by a whole multiple of W, so
// through this world's own transform they land edge-butted with no resample:
//   dem-tight-w [-3510.31,-2110.33] | dem-tight-e [-2110.33,-710.35] | rd-tight [-710.35,689.64]
// Measured agreement across the shared edges, two independent 3DEP exports of
// the same lidar read one cell either side:
//   dem-tight-e | red-dog/dem-tight   mean |dz| 0.348 m
//   dem-tight-w | dem-tight-e         mean |dz| 0.575 m
// upper/dem-wide vs red-dog/dem-wide over their 1485 x 3200 m overlap: 0.050 m.
//
// STACK ORDER (ground.mjs): these three are applied BENEATH kt22/dem-tight and
// red-dog/dem-tight. Wherever the merged world already read a tight frame it
// still reads exactly that frame, so nothing the merge verified moves.
//
// Row 0 = SOUTH edge, +x east. Values are DECIMETRES relative to z0 = 1890.0 m.
// Same world frame and transform as dem-data.mjs / dem-kt.mjs: ENU ground
// metres about 39.19197,-120.23108, x = (merc_x - merc_x0)*cos(lat0).//
// CROPPED by poi-lab tools/export-red-dog (specs/0001 D13/D41):
//   DEM_UP_WIDE 512 -> 256 (2x, 512 KB -> 128 KB raw)
//   DEM_UP_W 1024 -> 256 (4x, 2048 KB -> 128 KB raw)
//   DEM_UP_E 1024 -> 256 (4x, 2048 KB -> 128 KB raw)
// Block-mean decimation. span / ox / oy are untouched, so every frame still
// registers 1:1 with the DEM stack; only the sample spacing changed.//
// DELTA-ENCODED by poi-lab tools/export-red-dog (specs/0049):
//   DEM_UP_WIDE 256x256 = 65,536 samples, round trip 0 mismatches
//   DEM_UP_W 256x256 = 65,536 samples, round trip 0 mismatches
//   DEM_UP_E 256x256 = 65,536 samples, round trip 0 mismatches
// Each frame's b64 now holds the 2-D predictor residual r = v - (left + up -
// upleft) as the same little-endian int16, and carries d: 2 to say so.
// scene/ground.mjs's decode() reverses it in raster order before anything
// else in this world sees a height. LOSSLESS: int16 wraparound is a bijection,
// and the build re-decoded every sample above to prove it. span / n / ox / oy
// and the export names are untouched, so every consumer registers 1:1.


export const DEM_UP_WIDE = { span: 3600.0, n: 256, ox: -2167.26, oy: -219.30, d: 2, b64: "" };
export const DEM_UP_W = { span: 1400.0, n: 256, ox: -2810.32, oy: -85.72, d: 2, b64: "" };
export const DEM_UP_E = { span: 1400.0, n: 256, ox: -1410.34, oy: -85.72, d: 2, b64: "" };

// ------------------------------------------------------- ESCALATION 1 patch
// `pois/palisades-upper/README.md` §3/§9 escalates a defect in the MERGED
// world's own elevation data: pois/red-dog-palisades/dem-wide.tif carries spike
// pixels on the KT-22 south side reading up to 225 m below their neighbours.
// This world reads that raster for terrain-mid, terrain-wide and the massif
// bridge, and groundZ() is bilinear — a 3.1 m pit drags every vertex within
// 3.1 m of it, and props are placed with groundZ.
//
// 12 pixels deviate more than 25 m below their own 5x5 median. Each is repaired
// with an INDEPENDENT 3DEP export's reading of the same ground where one covers
// it (this bundle's dem-tight-s / dem-tight-e / dem-wide, or kt22/dem-tight),
// and with the 5x5 median only where none does. Flat index into the 1024^2
// dem-wide array, then decimetres relative to 1890.0 m — applied in ground.mjs
// at decode. Generated by work/bake_dem_upper.py; the per-pixel table with its
// provenance is work/dem-upper.json.
export const DEM_WIDE_PATCH = [189865,3491,190889,3290,221380,4397,221381,4384,222404,4424,222405,4407,331984,4480,331985,4499,333008,4483,333009,4503,334032,4488,334033,4504];
export default { DEM_UP_WIDE, DEM_UP_W, DEM_UP_E, DEM_WIDE_PATCH };
